<title>USA: Cyclone threat to ships in Southern Indian Ocean.</title>
<headline>Cyclone threat to ships in Southern Indian Ocean.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Karlette, is posing a threat to shipping in the southern Indian Ocean near 34s/59e, Independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Karlette has winds of 40 mph and is moving south southeast at 20 mph. It is expected to turn southeast and increase its forward speed, becoming extratropical in about 24 hours.</p>
